spes therm: read the RTC counter twice (0221, read only).

all-13 (spestherm=1): one of twelve 30-second lines showed "rtc 17023242" (0x0103c0ca) between 245996 and 246056; every SPMI
read had reported success and the LSB check (as Linux qpnp-rtc) passed. spes_therm_rtc_read now reads the four bytes a second
time and accepts the value only if the second reading is the same or one second later; otherwise it tries again (three
attempts as before). Still observer reads of 0x6048..0x604b only. The cause of the wrong bytes is not known yet.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/spes_therm.c b/bsd/dev/spes_therm.c
index 5cbdd0e..cb143cb 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/spes_therm.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/spes_therm.c
@@ -195,6 +195,21 @@ spes_therm_rtc_read(uint32_t *secs, uint8_t *ctrl_out)
 			return -1;
 		}
 		if (spes_rtc_read_consistent(b[0], lsb)) {
+			/*
+			 * 0221: all-13 logged one counter of 0x0103c0ca between 0x0003c0ec and 0x0003c128 (three
+			 * of the four bytes wrong, each read reported success). Read the four bytes a second time
+			 * and take the value only when the counter did not move by more than a second.
+			 */
+			uint8_t c[4] = {0, 0, 0, 0};
+			bool again = true;
+			for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+				if (sweet_spmi_read(SPES_THERM_SID, SPES_RTC_RDATA0 + i, &c[i]) != 0) {
+					again = false;
+				}
+			}
+			if (!again || spes_rtc_assemble(c) - spes_rtc_assemble(b) > 1u) {
+				continue;
+			}
 			*secs = spes_rtc_assemble(b);
 			if (ctrl_out) {
 				*ctrl_out = ctrl;
